1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,400
Hello and welcome back to JD Science.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:05,280
Today we are exploring reproduction.

3
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:09,740
Human egg and sperm cells each have 23 chromosomes.

4
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:14,560
When they fuse, the zygote has 46 chromosomes, which

5
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:15,860
are 23 pairs.

6
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:19,700
Mitosis makes identical cells for growth and repair.

7
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:24,340
Myosis makes gametes with half the chromosomes and each gamete

8
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:25,580
is genetically different.

9
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:30,220
Sexual reproduction needs two parents and produces variation.

10
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:34,500
Asexual reproduction needs one parent and produces clones.

11
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:39,360
Genes are sections of DNA on chromosomes and each gene

12
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:40,680
codes for a protein.

13
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:45,120
DNA is a double helix made of nucleotides and bases

14
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:48,200
pair as C with G and A with T.

15
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:52,380
For genetics, each parent passes on one allele of each

16
00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:52,880
gene.

17
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:56,740
Dominant alleles show up even when only one copy is

18
00:00:56,740 --> 00:00:57,180
present.

19
00:00:57,740 --> 00:01:00,760
Recessive alleles only show when two copies are present.

20
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:03,260
Cystic fibrosis is recessive.

21
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:05,160
Polydactyly is dominant.

22
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,700
Sex is determined by the X and Y chromosomes.

23
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:13,360
Myosis reduces chromosome number and generates genetic variation

24
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:17,060
through processes including recombination and independent

25
00:01:17,060 --> 00:01:17,620
assortment.

26
00:01:18,420 --> 00:01:21,360
Fertilization restores the diploid chromosome number.

27
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:25,140
In inheritance questions, always define the allele

28
00:01:25,140 --> 00:01:27,780
symbols before completing a Punnett square.

29
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:31,480
A dominant allele is expressed in a heterozygote.

30
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:35,340
This does not mean it is necessarily more common in the population.

31
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,880
As you revise this topic, try to explain the key process in

32
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:40,820
your own words.

33
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:45,080
Focus on what happens, why it happens, and how the structures

34
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:46,960
involved help the process work.

35
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:50,680
Now pause the video and try this exam style

36
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:51,220
question.

37
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:55,380
A woman is heterozygous for cystic fibrosis, F, and a

38
00:01:55,380 --> 00:01:57,500
man does not carry the allele FF.

39
00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:01,720
Using a Punnett square, work out the probability that their child

40
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:03,100
has cystic fibrosis.

41
00:02:03,480 --> 00:02:05,580
Use F for the recessive allele.

42
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:07,340
Here is a model answer.

43
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:12,900
ParentsFFF gives offspring FFFFFF.

44
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:16,640
The child has cystic fibrosis only if FF.

45
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:20,000
Probability equals sign 0%.

46
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,900
If this explanation has helped, please subscribe to JD

47
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:25,400
Science for more lessons.

48
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:29,620
You can find further learning resources and practice questions at

49
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:34,040
jdscience .co

50
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:34,780
.uk.

51
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:36,420
Thank you for watching.

